        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "92b080f9-4d7e-5205-a567-d4a96697b20c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marvin Cohen, Wallace Shawn, Richard Dreyfuss, Keith Carradine, Jill Eikenberry, Larry Pine, Mimi Kennedy, Louis Malle\n- Works: The Don Juan and the Non-Don Juan, My Dinner with Andre, The Princess Bride, The Haunted Mansion, Toy Story franchise, The Incredibles\n- Organizations: New York Shakespeare Festival, Poets at the Public Series\n- Roles: actor, voice actor, playwright, essayist, comedian, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Marvin Cohen's 1980 play \"The Don Juan and the Non-Don Juan\" was first performed at the New York Shakespeare Festival as part of the Poets at the Public Series.\n- Staged readings of Marvin Cohen's play \"The Don Juan and the Non-Don Juan\" featured Richard Dreyfuss, Keith Carradine, Wallace Shawn, Jill Eikenberry, Larry Pine, and Mimi Kennedy.\n- Wallace Michael Shawn was born on November 12, 1943, and is an American actor, voice actor, playwright, essayist, and comedian.\n- Wallace Shawn played Wally Shawn in Louis Malle's 1981 comedy-drama \"My Dinner with Andre.\"\n- Wallace Shawn played Vizzini in \"The Princess Bride\" in 1987.\n- Wallace Shawn voiced Rex in the \"Toy Story\" franchise and Gilbert Huph in \"The Incredibles\" in 2004.\n- Wallace Shawn also played Ezra in \"The Haunted Mansion.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4b9a14c0-62c2-51cf-a47f-9ae2b0ae31b8",
        "text": "Page: Marvin Cohen (American writer). Sentence: His 1980 play \"The Don Juan and the Non-Don Juan\" was first performed at the New York Shakespeare Festival as part of the Poets at the Public Series.\nPage: Marvin Cohen (American writer). Sentence: Staged readings of the play have featured actors Richard Dreyfuss, Keith Carradine, Wallace Shawn, Jill Eikenberry, Larry Pine, and Mimi Kennedy.\nPage: Wallace Shawn. Sentence: Wallace Michael Shawn (born November 12, 1943) is an American actor, voice actor, playwright, essayist and comedian.\nPage: Wallace Shawn. Sentence: His film roles have included those of Wally Shawn in the Louis Malle-directed comedy-drama \"My Dinner with Andre\" (1981), Vizzini in \"The Princess Bride\" (1987), Ezra in \"The Haunted Mansion\", providing the voice of Rex in the \"Toy Story\" franchise, providing the voice of Gilbert Huph in \"The Incredibles\" (2004), and providing the voice of Calico in \"\" (2010).",
